10. Allergy to the investigational drug or any of its components and/or history of severe allergic reaction to the drug or allergens (such as allergic asthma);
11. Any major disease or unstable disease state (such as unstable angina pectoris, myocardial infarction or coronary revascularization, heart failure, acute and chronic renal failure, chronic liver disease, severe lung disease, blood Diabetic patients with disease, poor blood sugar control, chronic infection in the past 2 years, received surgical treatment 7 days ago, advanced cardiac insufficiency (NYHA stage IV), major depressive episode, etc.);
