13. HIV, hepatitis C or Treponema pallidum antibody test positive, hepatitis B surface antigen positive (except hepatitis B carriers);
14. History of physical examination or imaging examination of neurological diseases (such as severe cerebrovascular disease, inflammation, infectious diseases and degenerative diseases, etc.);
15. History of severe craniocerebral injury, craniocerebral surgery or intracranial hematoma with permanent brain injury;
